  "id": "EUVD-2026-136593",
  "enisaUuid": "b5e492b3-157a-3b3b-bb56-48a9b9573455",
  "description": "Traefik before 2.11.62, 3.x before 3.7.18, and 3.8.0-rc.1 contain an authorization bypass because the sanitizePath entry point option leaves dot-segments carrying path parameters, such as /..;x/, unresolved when matching routers and applying middlewares. Unauthenticated attackers can send requests like /public/..;x/admin to a parameter-stripping backend shared with a protected router, bypassing authentication or authorization middlewares to reach protected resources.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 26, 2026, 4:01:24 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 26, 2026, 4:01:24 PM",
